     "title": "The Skill That Can't Be Prompted: Why AI Makes Engineering Judgment the Scarce Resource",
     "thesis": "As AI takes over first-draft code, the skills worth building on demand are the ones AI can't supply and actively erodes, namely review, verification, system design and debugging, so teams that treat 'learn it when you need it' as a plan for judgment will end up with engineers who can't catch what the machines get wrong.",
